**Session end 2026-08-25 (seventh session).** Branch `polar-average-perf` still at
**3429f59f**, `src/` clean, nothing committed this session -- the work was experimental,
not code. **ONE JOB QUEUED: 11009786** on `apu1` (pending on priority; apu1 was fully
allocated all session).

**START HERE: [[dhj-floors-for-1e-6-bar]].** The user asked what floors and `max_eta` to
use for the dhj run with tabulated EOS + correlated-k, then asked me to test it (hydro
only), varying floors and `x1max`, with the goal "include the 1e-6 bar level but keep the
timestep large". Measured on apudev, production grid, ~1 rotation per arm.

**The answer is one parameter: `pfloor = 1.0e-3`, not 1.0.** Units are cgs, so
1 barye = 1e-6 bar exactly -- the old floor pinned the top 7 cells at precisely
p = 1.000e-06 bar / 2159.9 K. It did not miss the level, it manufactured it. Costs 0.2 %
in cycles. `x1max` must NOT be extended and `dfloor` must NOT be raised; both are
measured dead ends, reasons in the memory. `tfloor_kelvin = 50` crashes the run.

**Job 11009786** = `/viper/u2/jinma/ATHENAK/bench/ck_hydro_long`, a long confirmation run
(pure hydro, tabulated EOS, correlated-k, the recommended floors), set up on the
`xe_long` pattern: own `athena` snapshot, `BUILD_COMMIT.txt`, `NOTES.md`, and
`resubmit_viper.sh` for each 24 h timeout. **When picking up: check it started, then check
`dhj.log` column `eos_efloor` is still 0** -- that is the tripwire saying pfloor is still
non-binding. If it fires, drop pfloor to 1e-4. Also watch mass drift in `dhj.hydro.hst`
(+0.061 % per rotation over the first rotation, not sustainable forever).

Two judgement calls I made without asking, both flagged to the user and easily changed:
the long run is **pure hydro** (that is what was validated; an MHD companion would add
`ohmic_resistivity = eos`, `max_eta = 1e13`, `bbot`), and `pfloor = 1e-3` is the measured
value rather than the safer-but-untested `1e-4`.

**Process lesson, cost a whole sweep:** my first sweep moved `pfloor`, `dfloor` AND
`tfloor_kelvin` together and all five arms died -- I could not tell which factor did it
and had to re-run everything with only `tfloor` restored. Also: I first told the user
`x1max` had to grow to 14.2e9, from the INITIAL condition. Wrong -- the atmosphere expands
and cools under correlated-k, and the evolved 1e-6 bar level is already inside the current
domain. **Measure the evolved state, not the IC.**

